---
.title = "Why AI can't replace humans...yet",
.author = "Jonathan Marler",
.date = @date("2026-05-18T00:00:00"),
.layout = "blogpost.shtml",
---

experience: AI have become a regular tool I reach for.  I use it for anything and everything that can make my life easier and make me more productive.  If I could use AI to generate all my code, I would. However, AI is far from being able to do that...so far.

Big Point:  small gaps in discernment over time create large gaps in quality

What is the Gap?

AI is like an army of new college graduates who studied every subject. They have an encyclopedic knowledge about everything with no real experience in anything. That gap is "experience".  Being a human, waking up in the morning, maitaining relationships with people, feeling joy, anger, all these things inform the way you live and work.

> NOTE: I notice some of the attributes we attribute to autism also apply to AI...only taken to the extreme
